# AI Chat Processing Rules

> Workflow-specific rules extending `obsidian-vault.mdc`

## Context

Rules for processing AI LLM chat exports (Perplexity, ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, Copilot) and extracting atomic knowledge notes. Applies when working with files in `04-RESOURCES/Integrations/Chats/`.

## Chat Storage Location

```
04-RESOURCES/Integrations/Chats/   - Raw AI chat exports with frontmatter
99-ARCHIVES/AI-Chats/              - Fully processed and archived chats
```

## Chat Naming Convention

Format: `{YYYY-MM-DD}_{Provider}_{Topic Slug}.md`

Examples:
- `2024-12-31_Perplexity_Information theory computational encoding.md`
- `2024-12-31_ChatGPT_React hooks best practices.md`
- `2024-12-31_Claude_Database schema design.md`

## Required Chat Frontmatter

All AI chat notes MUST include:

```yaml
---
creation_date: YYYY-MM-DD
modification_date: YYYY-MM-DD
author: Jimmy Briggs <jimmy.briggs@noclocks.dev>
description: Brief description of chat content
tags:
  - Type/Chat
  - Topic/{RelevantTopics}
  - Status/{Draft|Complete}
aliases:
  - Short reference name
publish: false
provider: Perplexity|ChatGPT|Claude|Cursor|Copilot|Other
chat_date: YYYY-MM-DD
extraction_status: pending|in_progress|complete
extracted_notes: []
topics: []
key_insights: []
---
```

## Extraction Status Values

- `pending` - Not yet processed
- `in_progress` - Currently being processed
- `complete` - All insights extracted

## Extractable Note Types

When processing chats, extract into these note types:

| Content Type | Note Type | Location |
|--------------|-----------|----------|
| Term/Concept definitions | `Definition - {Term}.md` | `04-RESOURCES/Definitions/Dictionary/` |
| Acronyms | `Definition - {Full Name (ACRONYM)}.md` | `04-RESOURCES/Definitions/Acronyms/` |
| Code examples | `Code - {Lang} - {Desc}.md` | `04-RESOURCES/Code/{Language}/` |
| How-to procedures | `Guide - {Topic}.md` | `04-RESOURCES/Guides/` |
| Tool/Resource lists | `List - {Category}.md` | `04-RESOURCES/Lists/` |
| Pure insights/ideas | `{Concept Name}.md` | `01-SLIPBOX/` |

## Extracted Note Requirements

All notes extracted from chats MUST include:

1. `source_chat` frontmatter field linking back to original chat
2. `source_provider` field indicating the AI provider
3. `confidence` field (high|medium|low) indicating reliability
4. Proper Topic tags matching relevant MOCs
5. Backlinks Dataview query

## Processing Workflow

1. **Capture**: Import raw chat with proper frontmatter
2. **Evaluate**: Identify extractable insights, mark `extraction_status: in_progress`
3. **Process**: Create atomic notes for each insight, update `extracted_notes` array
4. **Archive**: Mark `extraction_status: complete`, optionally move to archives

## Tag Matching for MOCs

Use spaced topic tags to match MOC Dataview queries:
- `Topic/Information Theory` (not `Topic/InformationTheory`)
- `Topic/Computer Science` (not `Topic/ComputerScience`)
- `Topic/Quantum Mechanics` (not `Topic/QuantumMechanics`)

## Quality Guidelines

When extracting insights:
- Each note should be atomic (one concept)
- Verify factual claims before marking high confidence
- Cross-link related extracted notes
- Add to relevant MOCs via proper Topic tags
- Include sufficient context without copying entire chat
